--  Read by two conformance cases: one that lets this shell capture all of it,
--  and one that sets a limit it goes past.
--
--  Sixteen thousand lines of a hundred characters is a little over a mebibyte,
--  which is the smallest `read.limit` a user can set.
for Line in 1 .. 16_000 loop
   put_line ("0123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789");
end loop;

put_line ("that was all of it");
quit (0);
